hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3076","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bashshar, narrated to us Abu Bakr al-Hanafi, narrated to us Aflah, who said: I heard al-Qasim ibn Muhammad narrate from 'Aishah (RA), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entered upon me while I was weeping. He said: \"What is the matter with you?\" She said: \"I am not praying.\" He said: \"That will not harm you. You are only one of the daughters of Adam; Allah has decreed upon you what He has decreed upon them.\" Then he mentioned the hadith until he said: \"Until we descended at al-Muhassab and we dismounted with him. He then called 'Abdur-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr and said: 'Take your sister out, and let her perform 'Umrah.'\"\n\n**CHAPTER:**"
